Below is an explanation of what’s happening and the one-line patch that fixes it.

1. Bug scenario & root cause  
   When you use a custom `loader` on a `VectorSource`, OpenLayers internally calls your loader function, then fires the `featuresloadend` event immediately after that. In the stock `xhr()` loader (in `src/ol/featureloader.js`), the code did:
   ```js
   if (success !== undefined) {
     success(features);
   }
   source.addFeatures(features);
   ```
   That means your `success` callback (which in turn fires `featuresloadend`) ran **before** the features were actually added to the source. At that moment the source is still empty, so calls like `getExtent()` return `[Infinity, Infinity, -Infinity, -Infinity]`.

2. Fix  
   Simply swap the two calls so that we add the features first, then call `success(...)`. Below is the minimal *SEARCH/REPLACE* edit.

```javascript
### src/ol/featureloader.js
<<<<<<< SEARCH
      function (features, dataProjection) {
        if (success !== undefined) {
          success(features);
        }
        source.addFeatures(features);
      },
=======
      function (features, dataProjection) {
        source.addFeatures(features);
        if (typeof success === 'function') {
          success(features);
        }
      },
>>>>>>> REPLACE
```
